  "icon": "FileCheck2",
  "estMinutes": 12,
  "title": "Get the teljesitesigazolas signed and invoice the period",
  "desc": "Register the contract, measure the period tetel by tetel, get the muszaki ellenor to sign the teljesitesigazolas, raise the szamla against it and let the module count the days the payment rules allow, so a refusal to certify is a dated fact with a forum rather than a stalemate.",
  "longDesc": "Hungarian construction payment turns on the teljesitesigazolas, and the reason it matters is that the contractor cannot lawfully invoice without one. That gives the certifying party a great deal of leverage and creates the failure everybody in the chain recognises: work is finished, nobody disputes it was finished, and the certificate does not arrive. The law answers that with a dedicated expert body rather than a lawsuit, but the answer is only available to a contractor who can show what was submitted, when, and what came back. Kept as the period runs, that record is a filing. Reconstructed afterwards it is an argument.",
